```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>DVD Logo Bounce</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            background-color: #000;
            overflow: hidden;
        }
        .dvd-logo {
            position: absolute;
            white-space: nowrap;
            color: #fff;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            font-size: 48px;
            font-weight: bold;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            text-shadow: 0 0 5px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="dvd-logo">DVD VIDEO</div>

    <script>
        const logo = document.querySelector('.dvd-logo');

        // Starting position and velocity
        let x = Math.random() * (window.innerWidth - 200);
        let y = Math.random() * (window.innerHeight - 60);
        let vx = (Math.random() * 4 + 2) * (Math.random() < 0.5 ? -1 : 1);
        let vy = (Math.random() * 4 + 2) * (Math.random() < 0.5 ? -1 : 1);

        function animate() {
            // Update position
            x += vx;
            y += vy;

            // Get logo dimensions for accurate collision detection
            const width = logo.offsetWidth;
            const height = logo.offsetHeight;

            // Bounce off left and right walls
            if (x <= 0) {
                x = 0;
                vx = Math.abs(vx);
            } else if (x + width >= window.innerWidth) {
                x = window.innerWidth - width;
                vx = -Math.abs(vx);
            }

            // Bounce off top and bottom walls
            if (y <= 0) {
                y = 0;
                vy = Math.abs(vy);
            } else if (y + height >= window.innerHeight) {
                y = window.innerHeight - height;
                vy = -Math.abs(vy);
            }

            // Apply new position
            logo.style.left = x + 'px';
            logo.style.top = y + 'px';

            requestAnimationFrame(animate);
        }

        animate();
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

This HTML file features:
- A "DVD VIDEO" text logo that moves in a straight line without gravity
- Bounces off all four walls and continues traveling in the opposite direction
- Uses `requestAnimationFrame` for smooth animation
- Random starting position and velocity on page load
